Course Prerequisite System
Description
Course Prerequisite System
Scenario: You're designing a university course system where courses have prerequisites. Edges go from prerequisite → dependent course.

Your Tasks:
Create a course dependency graph with 6 courses (0-5)

Add prerequisites: Course 1 needs Course 0, Course 2 needs Course 0, Course 3 needs Course 1 and 2, Course 4 needs Course 2, Course 5 needs Course 3 and 4

Determine all prerequisites (direct and indirect) for Course 5

Find all courses that are directly required for Course 3

Check if the graph has a cycle (circular dependencies)

If there's no cycle, perform topological sort to find the order to take courses

Find all courses that have no prerequisites (can be taken first)

Count how many courses directly depend on Course 2


====================================
Course Prerequisite System
====================================

1. All prerequisites of Course 5
3, 1, 0, 2, 4

2. Direct prerequisites of Course 3
1, 2

3. Cycle Detection
No Cycle Found

4. Topological Sort
0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5

5. Courses without prerequisites
0

6. Direct dependents of Course 2
2

====================================
